☐ Focused tests pass.
☐ The complete unit suite passes.
☐ No unit test claims to verify DFHack runtime behavior.

## Phase 6: Live DFHack acceptance

☐ Extend the existing non-owning native-screen specification instead of
  creating a separate owned screen or direct-callback harness.
☐ Establish the required real base-game menu through normal DFHack input.
☐ Resolve a stable base-game control through a complete `main_interface` path
  without `native_root`.
☐ Resolve and inspect a real `info.creatures` list row through the structural
  and widget path proven in Phase 0.
☐ Verify the returned raw value is the same native userdata identity resolved
  by direct DFHack APIs.
☐ Verify text and bounds from the DwarfSpec subject against the live control.
☐ Place the pointer within the resolved row's rendered bounds.
☐ Dispatch one safe, reversible input through the subject and prove an
  observable base-game response.
☐ Call `ds.redraw()` and prove completed rendering through the native observer.
☐ Prove the viewscreen, focus list, and screen stack remain unchanged by
  mounting and querying.
☐ Restore the original menu, pointer state, instrumentation, and test fixture
  state during cleanup.
☐ Record unit, live-host, and cleanup evidence separately.

Exit gate:

☐ At least one full `main_interface` path and one real widget-backed list-row
  scenario pass against a supported DFHack host.
☐ Cleanup verification passes even if lookup, input, or assertion is injected
  to fail.
☐ No coordinate-only lookup is accepted as evidence for widget resolution.

## Phase 7: Public contract and documentation

☐ Update `src/ds.d.lua` to document full native game-UI paths.
☐ Document the structural-field-to-widget transition rule.
☐ Document the dual-root compatibility and ambiguity behavior.
☐ Document that `ds.root()` remains the exact viewscreen widget root.
☐ Present full game-UI paths as the common base-game testing API.
☐ Present `native_root` only as an advanced ambiguity or compatibility escape
  hatch.
☐ Add examples for:
  - a direct viewscreen-widget path;
  - `info.creatures`;
  - the verified `info.creatures` list-row path;
  - an explicit-root ambiguity resolution.
☐ Document that the current Hauling route rows are procedurally rendered and
